Subject: [PATCH] schemas: Don't cache the pending item array in xmlSchemaFixupComponents

xmlSchemaFixupComponents stored con->pending->items in a local variable and
iterated over it in a series of loops. Some fixup functions add components to
the pending list: xmlSchemaFixupSimpleTypeStageTwo fixes up the base type of a
simple type, and if that base is (wrongly) a complex type,
xmlSchemaFixupComplexType creates a particle and a model group for it, which
can reallocate the array. The following iterations then read the freed array
(heap-use-after-free). The complex type loop already reads
con->pending->items[i] directly; do the same in all loops and drop the cached
pointer.

Found with the schema fuzzer (heap-use-after-free in xmlSchemaFixupComponents;
on wasm32 the stale entries trap with an out-of-bounds load). Fuzzing builds
grow the list one item at a time, so any schema with a simple type restricting
a mixed complex type triggers it there. Regression test
test/schemas/pendingrealloc_0.xsd (ten pending components, the default
initial list size).

Not fixed upstream as of 21c8223.
Upstream: issue GNOME/libxml2#1104 (Trail of Bits, 2026-04-23) reported this
use-after-free and proposed the same change; it was closed on 2026-05-29
without a fix.
---
diff --git a/result/schemas/pendingrealloc_0_0.err b/result/schemas/pendingrealloc_0_0.err
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..14aa083
--- /dev/null
+++ b/result/schemas/pendingrealloc_0_0.err
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+./test/schemas/pendingrealloc_0.xsd:7: element simpleType: Schemas parser error : simple type 's': The base type 'c' is not a simple type.
diff --git a/test/schemas/pendingrealloc_0.xml b/test/schemas/pendingrealloc_0.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..69d62f2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/schemas/pendingrealloc_0.xml
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+<doc/>
diff --git a/test/schemas/pendingrealloc_0.xsd b/test/schemas/pendingrealloc_0.xsd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c2f2d50
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/schemas/pendingrealloc_0.xsd
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+<?xml version="1.0"?>
+<!-- The fixup of the simple type "s" fixes up its complex base type "c",
+     which adds a particle and a model group to the pending component list.
+     With ten components pending, this reallocates the list while
+     xmlSchemaFixupComponents iterates over it. -->
+<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
+  <xs:simpleType name="s"><xs:restriction base="c"/></xs:simpleType>
+  <xs:complexType name="c" mixed="true"/>
+  <xs:complexType name="c1"/>
+  <xs:complexType name="c2"/>
+  <xs:complexType name="c3"/>
+  <xs:complexType name="c4"/>
+  <xs:complexType name="c5"/>
+  <xs:complexType name="c6"/>
+  <xs:complexType name="c7"/>
+  <xs:complexType name="c8"/>
+</xs:schema>
